 # ASC Admin UI
 
-Web-based administration panel for managing organizations, workspaces, teams, users, and invitations.
+Administration for organisations, workspaces, teams, people, access and operations. Every tool is available from the grouped sidebar, the searchable overview and the command search (Ctrl+K or Cmd+K).
 
-This replaces the `asccli` command-line tool, which has been removed.
+## Feature directory
 
-## Features
+| Area | Tool | Existing functionality |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Organisation and teams | [Organisations](src/pages/organizations.ts) | Organisation creation, membership and settings; detail pages include workspaces and organisation administration. |
+| Organisation and teams | [Workspaces](src/pages/workspaces.ts) | Workspace hierarchy, creation and detail settings, membership and child teams. |
+| Organisation and teams | [Teams](src/pages/teams.ts) | Team creation, membership, invitations and settings. |
+| Organisation and teams | [Organisation directory](src/pages/external-structure.ts) | External organisational structures and directory mappings. |
+| People and access | [Users](src/pages/users.ts) | Search and filter accounts by role, status, verification and two-factor setup; review sessions and account security. |
+| People and access | [Invitations](src/pages/invitations.ts) | Personal invitations and organisation, workspace and team invitation management. |
+| People and access | [Permissions](src/pages/permissions.ts) | Member and team permissions, role assignments and access exceptions. |
+| People and access | [Custom roles](src/pages/custom-roles.ts) | Scoped custom role definitions and permission rules. |
+| People and access | [Permission presets](src/pages/permission-presets.ts) | Reusable permission configurations. |
+| People and access | [Built-in roles](src/pages/system-roles.ts) | Built-in role and permission reference. |
+| Operations | [Content](src/pages/cms.ts) | CMS content, menus and branding. |
+| Operations | Support tickets | Federated staff support desk from `@asc/support-host`: triage, assignment and ticket detail. |
+| Operations | [Plugin review](src/pages/plugin-review.ts) | Publisher and extension review, approval and platform controls. |
+| Operations | [System administration](src/pages/system-admin.ts) | System user administration, subject to the existing system access gate. |
 
-- **Organizations**: Create and manage organizations with namespaces
-- **Workspaces**: Create workspaces within organizations
-- **Teams**: Create and manage teams within organizations
-- **Users**: Manage user memberships across organizations, workspaces, and teams
-- **Invitations**: Send, view, resend, and cancel organization invitations
-- **System Admin**: Manage system administrators
+The overview shows organisation memberships and pending invitations for the signed-in person. A failed request appears as unavailable rather than zero. Refresh retries the summary. Scope links open the selected organisation, workspace or team; the account menu changes scope.
+
+Pins are stored per user in this browser and contain only tool identifiers. Search matches titles, descriptions and task keywords. The directory is also available as `@asc/ui/feature-directory` and the `FeatureDirectory` JSON-render component.
+
+## Access
+
+Navigation does not grant permissions. The Better Auth permission plugin, service checks and database row and field controls remain authoritative. System administration follows `canAccessHiddenSystemFeatures`; other tools apply their existing page and operation checks.
 
 ## Development
 
-```bash
-bun install
-bun dev
-```
+Run the existing development stack from the repository root. The admin frontend is selected with `-F admin-ui`; it uses the authentication service and the services for the features being exercised. Support additionally needs its federated frontend. Do not start a second copy of a running stack.
 
-The app will be available at http://localhost:3015
+The default development address is http://localhost:3015. The application reads its configured service URLs at boot; see [the build configuration](rsbuild.config.ts) and [environment example](.env.example).
 
-## Environment
+From this directory:
 
-Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and configure:
+```sh
+bun run check-types
+bun run build
+```
 
-- `AUTH_BASE_URL`: Backend authentication service URL
-- `SURREALDB_ENDPOINT`: SurrealDB connection URL
-- `BACKEND_ORIGIN`: Backend service origin
-- `JWKS_PATH`: JWKS endpoint for JWT validation
+The focused browser regression is [13-admin-overview.spec.ts](../../../e2e/specs/13-admin-overview.spec.ts). Run it from `e2e` using the repository's isolated test stack and authenticated setup. Shared UI builds must finish before starting browser tests.
